WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.640
- So it's treason then.

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.120
(lightsaber whirs)
(lightsaber hums)

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:06.900
Or at least that's what a lot
of people are worried about.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.760
People are rightfully upset
about the Trump campaign

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.650
and the Trump administration's attempts

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:15.840
to effectively overthrow the
results of the 2020 election.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:16.960
So the question is,

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.470
and I never thought I'd
be asking this question,

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:20.990
did people commit sedition and treason

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:23.250
when they stormed the
Capitol on January 6th?

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.900
And more importantly, did some
of our elected politicians

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:28.470
actually commit sedition and treason?

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:32.102
And if they did, can they
be expelled from Congress?

00:00:32.102 --> 00:00:34.900
(dramatic music)

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.310
Sponsored by Skillshare.

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:38.040
Hey, legal eagles, it's time to think

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.590
like a national security lawyer,

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:41.320
and welcome to my new office,

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:44.860
with one of those incredibly
practical outward-facing desks.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.230
But it does allow me to do this,

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:48.180
(papers thump)

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.310
which adds quite a lot a lot of gravitas

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:51.660
to whatever I'm going to say.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.520
It's LegalEagle, now
with 7% more gravitas.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:58.210
But today, we're talking
about sedition and treason.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:01.210
Americans are trying to find
the right words to convey

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:04.060
just how desperate the Trump
administration's efforts are

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:06.700
to hold on to power, and
they've generally landed

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:09.230
on the concepts of treason and sedition.

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:10.870
But do they fit?

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.370
Well, let's start with what is treason?

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:14.850
The early Americans were men and women

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.800
who actually committed treason
against the English Crown.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:20.210
That's actually how this
country was founded.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:22.320
So they were bound to
have a pretty limited view

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.730
of what constituted an
offense against the state.

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:26.870
In their experience,
kings used treason charges

00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:28.350
to silence their political opponents

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:29.890
and to punish their enemies,

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:32.300
so they defined treason quite narrowly.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.060
Treason is in fact the only crime

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.720
described in the Constitution.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.767
Quote, "Treason against the
United States shall consist

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:39.847
"only in levying war against them,

00:01:39.847 --> 00:01:41.847
"or in adhering to their enemies,

00:01:41.847 --> 00:01:43.397
"giving them aid and comfort.

00:01:43.397 --> 00:01:45.277
"No person shall be convicted of treason

00:01:45.277 --> 00:01:47.757
"unless on the testimony of two witnesses

00:01:47.757 --> 00:01:51.110
"of the same overt act, or
on confession in open court."

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.510
This comes from the English
definition of treason.

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:56.770
In the 14th century, Edward
III's judges expanded

00:01:56.770 --> 00:01:58.120
the common law concept of treason

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:00.670
to cover just about anything
the king didn't like.

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:03.280
For example, if a person went
hunting on the king's forest

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.660
without permission, this was
treason, rather than trespass.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:10.090
That's a crime, but that
probably shouldn't be treason.

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:12.350
Therefore, the English
aristocracy compelled

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:14.400
Edward III to agree to
an act of parliament

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.830
that restricted the definition of treason

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:18.560
to a direct offense against
the king or his family,

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.050
such as acts of violence,
levying war against England,

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:23.550
and giving aid and comfort
to the king's enemies

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:25.450
in the English realm or elsewhere.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.990
And that's where we derive
the definition of treason

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:30.230
in the US Constitution, either levying war

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:32.930
against the United States,
or adhering to the enemies

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:35.030
of the United States, and
giving them aid and comfort,

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:37.130
which repeats an
interesting legal principle.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:39.950
The founders were simultaneously
disgusted by the monarchy,

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.640
but also guided by
English legal principles,

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:45.400
which takes us to the
affair of Aaron Burr.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.710
There actually haven't
been that many prosecutions

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:49.720
against politicians
for committing treason,

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:51.040
probably for good reason.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:53.740
But the most prominent politician
to be tried for treason

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.020
against the United States
is probably Aaron Burr,

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:57.220
former vice-president,

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:59.980
and the man who killed
Alexander Hamilton in a duel.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.780
After Burr killed Hamilton,

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.440
the political class
basically shunned Burr.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.030
But he wasn't willing to wait for it,

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:09.270
so Burr reached out to Great
Britain to offer his help

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:12.270
if they felt like annexing
the Western United States.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.360
The English royalty more
or less ignored Burr,

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:17.330
so he went on a recruiting
trip to Blennerhassett Island.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:20.380
Think of this as the
Mar-a-Lago of the Ohio River,

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:21.680
where he got financial backing

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.300
from a wealthy Irish immigrant.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.140
And Burr went to New Orleans
and enlisted the help

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.560
of basically rich guys and ex-politicians.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.080
The plot seemed to involve
annexing parts of Mexico

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:32.460
and Louisiana and convincing
other states to secede,

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:34.020
and start a new country.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.010
But Burr wasn't just talking trash.

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:38.550
His co-conspirator was
General James Wilkinson,

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:41.070
basically the Mike Flynn
of the 19th century.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.800
Wilkinson was the highest
ranking general in the Army,

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.100
and like Flynn, Wilkinson
was a secret agent

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.790
for a foreign government,
in his case, Spain.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:50.900
But unlike Flynn, nobody knew about

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.490
Wilkinson's treachery at the time.

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:54.130
Wilkinson was still on active duty

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:56.190
in command of Western soldiers.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:58.600
But after a year of planning,
Wilkinson backed out,

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.180
and alerted President Jefferson.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:01.590
Burr left Blennerhassett Island

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:04.440
with fewer than 100 supporters
and tried to escape.

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:07.070
He was eventually caught
and tried for treason.

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:10.300
But the trial was America's
first trial of the century.

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:13.030
Burr was defended by two
ex-attorneys general,

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:14.360
just think of them as the Bill Barr

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:15.760
and Jeff Sessions of the time.

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:18.090
And those lawyers argue that
the definition of treason

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.460
required evidence of an
overt act by the defendant

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:23.550
in furtherance of levying war
against the United States.

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:26.360
And Chief Justice Marshall
agreed with this interpretation.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:28.390
He ruled that Burr had
First Amendment right

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:30.200
to voice his opposition to the government,

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.033
to the president,

00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:33.120
and to the very concept
of the United States.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.160
But Marshall's definition of
overt action was very narrow.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.747
Quote, "There must be an
actual assembling of men

00:04:38.747 --> 00:04:39.927
"for the treasonable purpose

00:04:39.927 --> 00:04:42.130
"to constitute a levying of war."

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:44.700
In his mind, talk without
assembling of men willing

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:47.060
to levy war was not actually treason,

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:48.870
and there was no question that Burr loved

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.730
to talk about schemes to take down the US,

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:52.770
and get back at his political rivals.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.520
There was a little doubt
that Burr had rallied

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:57.530
with volunteers and businessmen
who would back his venture.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.400
However, Burr wasn't physically present

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.690
on Blennerhassett Island
when his volunteers gathered

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:04.510
with weapons, and Justice
Marshall had already told the jury

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:06.240
that they couldn't
consider any actions of war

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.680
that occurred outside of
Blennerhassett Island.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:10.270
The prosecution could
not convince the jury

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:12.770
to hold Burr responsible for an overt act

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:15.010
taking up arms against America.

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:17.080
The jury found him not guilty.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:19.870
Burr's goals were still murky to this day,

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:21.360
largely because Burr said different things

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:22.420
to different people.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.180
On one day, he was trying to
colonize part of Louisiana,

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:27.180
the next, he was trying to
convince Western settlers

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.300
to revolt against the United
States, and the day after that,

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:32.110
he was hoping to wrangle
Texas away from Spain.

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:33.780
And while the elements
of treason can include

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:34.770
the breach of allegiance,

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.150
these actions were not
unanimously considered treason,

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:39.360
since plotting against
Spain was not exactly

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.960
a betrayal of allegiance
to the United States.

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:44.220
And it wasn't entirely clear
that encouraging the states

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:47.470
to engage in another revolution
was illegal in 1805 either.

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:49.830
But the Burr prosecution
was the exception,

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:50.700
rather than the rule.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:52.560
There have been fewer
than 30 treason charges

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:55.310
since the Constitution
was ratified in 1789.

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:57.190
The people who conspired
with John Wilkes Booth

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.540
to kill President Lincoln were charged

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.930
with traitorous murder
and attempted murder.

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:02.640
People were charged with treason

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.900
for defecting to Nazi
Germany during World War II,

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:07.890
or aiding and abetting the
Japanese during the same period.

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:10.390
So the question is does
anything that President Trump

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:12.700
or his surrogates have said or done

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:14.830
rise to the level of treason?

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:17.930
Well, in a legal sense,
almost certainly not.

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:19.950
Now, arguably the closest
President Trump has ever come

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:22.380
to treason would be in
arguably collaborating

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.370
with a foreign government to
undermine the United States

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:26.280
through interfering with election.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:30.240
And while welcoming and
utilizing the resources

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.100
of a foreign government
in one's own election

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:36.490
is a lot of things, it's
probably not levying war,

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:38.260
and it's probably not treason.

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:40.670
And with respect to the
things that the president

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:42.440
and the president's
campaign have tried to do

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:45.460
with respect to undoing the
results of the 2020 election

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:47.750
through petitioning the courts,

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:50.530
most of what they have done
explicitly seeks to use

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:51.920
the force of the United States,

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:54.880
whether that use of force
is legitimate, or not.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.930
So he isn't levying war
against the United States.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.810
He's actually advocating for the use

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:02.040
of the implements of the
United States itself.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:04.910
So no matter how badly
you may think he has acted

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:07.010
in that context, and
you'd probably be right

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:08.650
that he's acted pretty poorly,

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:12.530
again, that's not levying war
against the United States.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.238
So it's not treason then.

00:07:14.238 --> 00:07:16.470
(lightsaber hums)
(lightsaber whirs)

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.240
But what about sedition?

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.450
America's second president,

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:22.790
John Adams, signed the
Sedition Act in 1798.

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:25.270
The Sedition Act made it a
crime for American citizens to,

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:27.617
quote, "Print, utter,
or publish any false,

00:07:27.617 --> 00:07:30.650
"scandalous, or malicious
writing about the government."

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:33.240
The Sedition Act was pretty
obviously unconstitutional

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:34.960
because it trampled on
the First Amendment right

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:37.710
to freedom of speech, but
Adams and his Federalist Party

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:39.620
went full steam ahead with prosecutions,

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:42.460
charging dozens of newspaper
editors with sedition.

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:44.770
Now, obviously, President Trump
would have loved this law,

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:47.120
since it gave him the
ability to jail reporters,

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:50.320
which he has many times advocated for.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:53.560
But the Americans of 1800,
however, did not love

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:55.040
the Sedition Act, and
punished the Federalists

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:57.930
by electing Thomas
Jefferson to the presidency.

00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:00.780
The original Sedition Act expired in 1801,

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:02.930
and the crime of sedition
has been severely limited

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:04.320
in the modern era.

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:07.230
Current laws on sedition
were passed in 1940.

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:08.990
A second sedition law punishes anyone

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:10.510
who advocates for the overthrow

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:12.500
of the federal government by force.

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:14.250
Now, the main distinction between sedition

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:17.760
and treason is that treason
requires levying, or waging war.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:20.930
Sedition can be language, or
conduct that incites people

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:24.030
to destroy, or overthrow,
or attack the government.

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:25.930
The Supreme Court upheld
the constitutionality

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:28.730
of the sedition laws, but
they're construed very narrowly

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:30.310
to prohibit the government from attacking

00:08:30.310 --> 00:08:32.120
purely political speech.

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:34.410
As currently interpreted,
sedition does not destroy

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.600
the First Amendment's
guarantee of freedom of speech.

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:39.130
Like treason, sedition
requires actively plotting

00:08:39.130 --> 00:08:41.650
to take up arms against the United States.

00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:45.070
Simply talking about it
on Parler is not enough.

00:08:45.070 --> 00:08:46.580
But if the Parler Patriots meet up

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:47.730
and plot to kill a governor,

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.700
or assassinate an incoming president,

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:51.760
they could be charged with sedition.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:53.880
And as the statute is
currently interpreted,

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:56.130
you actually have to plot to use force

00:08:56.130 --> 00:08:58.060
against the United States.

00:08:58.060 --> 00:09:00.690
And proving sedition is
harder than you might think.

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:03.300
For example, in 2014, a
Christian focus group known

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:06.810
as the Hutaree held military
training exercises in Michigan

00:09:06.810 --> 00:09:09.050
and amassed lots and lots of weapons.

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:10.830
They called themselves warriors for Jesus,

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:12.610
and were found in possession of tear gas,

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:14.580
night-vision goggles, a dagger, a sword,

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:17.940
manuals on bomb-making, books
by Hitler, race war books,

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:19.560
and a bunch of guns.

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:21.690
The FBI spent a year
infiltrating the group,

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:22.610
and eventually charged them

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:24.230
with plotting to kill a police officer

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:27.360
and ambush several more
officers at a funeral.

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:29.220
But a federal judge acquitted all of them,

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:31.710
because they were engaged
in political speech.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:32.917
The judge said that, quote,

00:09:32.917 --> 00:09:34.550
"There was something fishy going on,"

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.860
but since something fishy isn't illegal,

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:38.520
the charges were dismissed.

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:40.920
The Hutaree argued that
their training exercises were

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:45.400
just some dudes playing with
guns in the woods, as one does.

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.680
The judge never bought into
the government's case that

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:49.920
they were going to actually commit crimes.

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:52.170
But some people actually
have been prosecuted

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:53.930
and convicted of sedition.

00:09:53.930 --> 00:09:56.190
For example, Sheikh Omar Abdel-Rahman,

00:09:56.190 --> 00:09:58.190
a blind Egyptian cleric,
living in New Jersey,

00:09:58.190 --> 00:10:00.820
who is now serving a
life sentence in prison.

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:02.670
Rahman and nine other men were convicted

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:03.820
of seditious conspiracy,

00:10:03.820 --> 00:10:06.580
despite committing no overt acts of war.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:08.940
However, Rahman was found
to have encouraged the men

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:10.900
to levy war against the United States.

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:13.160
The group was arrested
while mixing explosives

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:15.070
in a garage in Queens.

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:17.170
The sedition laws make speech criminal

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:19.230
only when the speech
constitutes an agreement

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:21.560
to use force against the United States.

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:23.410
So in case you currently live in Michigan,

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:26.150
or let's be honest, Florida,
here's how that would play out.

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:27.890
You can generally give an opinion that

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:30.840
the government should be
overthrown, even by violence.

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:33.350
You can advocate for
the forcible overthrow

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:35.120
of the government in the abstract.

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:36.850
But you can't explicitly encourage,

00:10:36.850 --> 00:10:38.760
or induce someone to
overthrow the government

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:40.620
by concrete action.

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:42.130
And it's not easy to tell

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:44.760
when speech plus action
crosses these lines.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:46.980
But to be convicted of
seditious conspiracy

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:49.790
under Section 2384, a
defendant has to conspire

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:53.000
to use force, not just
advocate the use of force.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:53.850
So with that background,

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:55.720
let's look at some of the
things that President Trump

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:57.040
and his surrogates have said,

00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:59.500
all of the beautiful
conversations that they've had

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:01.740
that were 100% perfect.

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:03.880
Well, during the first debate,
President Trump said that

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:05.870
the right-wing Proud Boy group should

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:07.490
stand back and stand by.

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:10.800
- Proud Boys, stand back, and stand by.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:12.690
- Some of the Proud
Boys viewed this comment

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:15.650
as a call to action, according
to extremist researchers.

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:18.280
The Proud Boys went on a rampage
in D.C. early in December

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:19.840
clashing with other protestors,

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:22.290
resulting in several people being stabbed.

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:25.060
Did President Trump
act like Sheikh Rahman?

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:26.410
No, not quite.

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:29.560
Were President Trump's words seditious?

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:30.410
Almost certainly not.

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:32.180
He was talking in the abstract,

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:33.520
and while we may hate that speech,

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:36.040
under the First Amendment,
we have to live with it,

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:37.850
and that's probably the better way.

00:11:37.850 --> 00:11:39.050
But let's talk about militias.

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:40.730
When a group of private
citizens gets together

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:42.250
to talk about hating the government,

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:45.560
and that group is armed, they
are often called militias.

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:48.000
But it's not illegal to create
a social group like this,

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.450
or even for them to call
themselves militias.

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:52.750
However, every state makes it
illegal for private militias

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:54.850
to in activities traditionally reserved

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:56.970
for authorized state militias.

00:11:56.970 --> 00:11:58.760
And frankly, states are pretty lax

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:00.310
in actually enforcing those laws,

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:02.790
which arguably leads to more
paranoid people gathering

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:05.110
with their guns and declaring
themselves as militias.

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:06.170
This might be harmless,

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:08.280
but the fact that there are
prominent people encouraging

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:10.240
this kind of activity
certainly doesn't help.

00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:12.060
And the people arrested in Michigan

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:13.590
for trying to kidnap the governor

00:12:13.590 --> 00:12:14.820
were charged with violating

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:16.500
Michigan's anti-terrorism statute,

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:18.170
rather than with sedition.

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:20.580
This is probably because
sedition's close association

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:23.170
with speed makes it really hard to prove.

00:12:23.170 --> 00:12:24.470
So you start to get the picture.

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:26.480
Prosecutors don't even
like to charge sedition,

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:28.590
because there are other
statutes that are a better fit,

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:30.220
and don't have the sort of issues

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:31.900
that you run into with
the First Amendment.

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:34.690
So you can see that charges of
sedition are incredibly rare,

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:36.520
and probably for good reason,

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:38.530
often not even being used against things

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:40.870
as extreme as an actual militia.

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:43.640
So things like filing a bogus lawsuit

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:45.490
to overturn an election,

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:48.330
not even going to come close
to actionable sedition,

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:50.550
though there are ways that
we might be able to punish

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:53.070
meritless lawsuits in different ways.

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:55.540
And similarly, challenging
the Electoral College results

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:58.540
through objections on
January 6th is not sedition,

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:00.890
because congresspeople
are simply following

00:13:00.890 --> 00:13:02.580
a constitutional mechanism,

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:04.050
or at least what they vehemently,

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:07.920
and wrongly, believe those
constitutional mechanisms to be.

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:10.440
Now, many of the Capitol rioters
are already being charged

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:11.480
with seditious conspiracy.

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:14.180
This is covered by 18 U.S.C. 2384.

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:16.580
The law gives prosecutors
a variety of ways

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:17.870
to charge these rioters.

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:19.877
For example, if two or
more people conspire

00:13:19.877 --> 00:13:22.680
"To prevent, hinder, or delay
the execution of any law,"

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:25.080
such as trying to stop
Congress from tabulating

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:26.660
the Electoral College votes,

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:29.230
this could be seditious conspiracy.

00:13:29.230 --> 00:13:31.410
I've covered this extensively
in another video about

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:33.440
all the crimes that the
Capitol rioters committed.

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:35.397
And likewise, if two
or more people, quote,

00:13:35.397 --> 00:13:38.150
"Seize, take, or possess any
property of the United States,"

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:41.400
such as, say, stealing mail,
computers, gavels, lecterns,

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:43.030
and other objects from the Capitol,

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:45.410
they could be charged under Section 2384,

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:47.460
in addition to being
charged with federal theft

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:48.790
and vandalism crimes.

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:50.670
Now, rioters can argue that

00:13:50.670 --> 00:13:52.310
they were there to peacefully protest,

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:55.060
and loudly expressing
one's opinion is protected

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:56.100
under the First Amendment,

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:59.410
even if a person generally
advocates for the use of force.

00:13:59.410 --> 00:14:01.070
There is a First Amendment
right to protest,

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:02.600
but there's not a First Amendment right

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:05.060
to stop the government from functioning.

00:14:05.060 --> 00:14:07.730
So if prosecutors can show that
they were engaged in action,

00:14:07.730 --> 00:14:10.750
not just speech, they can
probably prove sedition,

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:12.480
and there's plenty of
evidence of coordination

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:14.650
between members of this mob.

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:16.530
But what about members of Congress,

00:14:16.530 --> 00:14:18.820
and members of the
president's inner circle?

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:20.790
Can they charges for the encouragement

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:24.170
and participation of what
happened on January 6th?

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:26.100
Well, the answer is that it both depends,

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:27.810
and it's complicated, an answer that

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:30.630
I'm sure will thrill absolutely everyone.

00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:32.110
Now, to prove seditious conspiracy,

00:14:32.110 --> 00:14:33.940
there must be an agreement
between two or more people

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:36.010
who are working together
towards a common goal,

00:14:36.010 --> 00:14:37.350
but the goal doesn't need to be

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:39.830
specifically articulated or explicit.

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:41.840
This means that the
co-conspirators didn't need

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:43.170
to pinky swear that they were going

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:45.240
to barge into the Capitol
Building, steal things,

00:14:45.240 --> 00:14:47.220
threaten people, and beat up the cops.

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:49.310
Individual defendants can tacitly agree

00:14:49.310 --> 00:14:50.900
to a larger conspiracy if they knew,

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:53.030
or should have known,
that others were going

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:54.100
to take the same actions,

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:56.110
such as storming the Capitol Building.

00:14:56.110 --> 00:14:58.500
And it's worth remembering why
rioters stormed the building

00:14:58.500 --> 00:14:59.333
in the first place.

00:14:59.333 --> 00:15:00.810
They had the common goal of preventing,

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:03.210
hindering, or delaying Congress' counting

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:05.140
and certification of the electoral votes.

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:07.920
And it also seems like
they wanted to punish

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:09.560
Mike Pence and Nancy Pelosi

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:11.280
and anyone that they
could get their hands on.

00:15:11.280 --> 00:15:13.550
And while I wouldn't call
it overwhelming evidence,

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:16.160
there is certainly some
evidence of coordination

00:15:16.160 --> 00:15:17.980
with people fairly high
up in the government.

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:20.270
For example, President
Trump promoted the event,

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:22.300
and may have even met with
the leader of the Proud Boys

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:24.650
on December 12th, the day
after the Supreme Court

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:27.270
dismissed the Texas lawsuit
to overturn the election.

00:15:27.270 --> 00:15:30.110
Enrique Tarrio, the
leader of the Proud Boys,

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:32.157
posted on Parler, "Last minute invite

00:15:32.157 --> 00:15:33.947
"to an undisclosed location.

00:15:33.947 --> 00:15:35.350
"Wow, I'm in awe,"

00:15:35.350 --> 00:15:37.960
and he was at the entrance
to the White House.

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:40.440
Tarrio's second post
shows the main portico

00:15:40.440 --> 00:15:42.410
with the comment, "Never
thought I'd be here."

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:43.760
And while the White House
said that Tarrio was

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:46.300
just taking a public tour,
it didn't provide any proof

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:48.630
that Tarrio followed the
rules for White House visits,

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:51.050
which require applying at
least 21 days in advance,

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:52.650
and passing a background check.

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:54.540
Tarrio is a convicted felon,

00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:56.560
and we now know that his
group, the Proud Boys,

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:59.310
participated in the January 6th attack,

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:01.860
and not surprisingly, one
of them has been accused

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:04.770
of plotting to kill Nancy
Pelosi and Mike Pence.

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:07.030
And much of what we know
about the plot to overthrow

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:08.900
the government is from Ali Alexander,

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:10.390
a right-wing conspiracy theorist

00:16:10.390 --> 00:16:12.537
who led one of the Stop the Steal groups,

00:16:12.537 --> 00:16:15.530
and in a livestream video
after the January 6th attack,

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:17.070
Alexander said he planned the rally

00:16:17.070 --> 00:16:19.410
with three GOP representatives, Paul Gosar

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:22.310
and Andy Biggs of Arizona,
and Mo Brooks of Alabama.

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:26.470
- I was the person who came
up with the January 6th idea

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:29.030
with Congressman Gosar,
Congressman Mo Brooks,

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:31.330
and then Congressman Andy Biggs.

00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:32.280
- And this wasn't something that

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:34.147
Alexander came up with after the fact.

00:16:34.147 --> 00:16:36.270
"The Intercept" reported
that Alexander claimed

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:38.870
to be working with members
of Congress three times

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:43.150
before the rally happened on
December 21st, 28th, and 29th.

00:16:43.150 --> 00:16:44.870
Now, remember that, because
we'll get back to that

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:48.010
in just a second, but let's
talk about the element of force.

00:16:48.010 --> 00:16:50.760
Seditious conspiracy requires
that co-conspirators plan

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:54.310
to effectuate their illegal
ends by some unlawful means.

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:56.770
Co-conspirators need to have
considered the use of force,

00:16:56.770 --> 00:17:00.170
even though the ultimate goal
need not actually use force.

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:01.990
And the element of force
does not necessarily mean

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:04.590
engaging in explicitly violent activities.

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:06.140
The government can prove this element

00:17:06.140 --> 00:17:07.850
if the co-conspirators contemplated

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:10.920
the unlawful invasion of rights of others.

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:13.090
And in media appearances before the event,

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:15.830
Alexander raised the stakes
and predicted violence.

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:18.550
He first asserted that if
Biden's win was certified,

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:20.700
there would be slavery,
concentration camps,

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:22.380
serfdom, and death.

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:24.230
- If you do not stand up and fight now,

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:29.230
you are signing your road,
and your ticket to serfdom.

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:31.060
- Alexander was very clear about

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:32.900
what he intended to do on January 6th,

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:34.240
to stop this from happening.

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:35.717
Quote, "Everyone can guess what me

00:17:35.717 --> 00:17:38.617
"and 500,000 others will
do to that building.

00:17:38.617 --> 00:17:41.870
"1776 is always an option."

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:44.600
And on January 5th, Alexander
led Trump supporters

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:46.930
in a peaceful rally on Freedom Plaza,

00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:47.944
where he shouted-

00:17:47.944 --> 00:17:49.942
- Victory or death!

00:17:49.942 --> 00:17:51.640
Victory-
- Or death!

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:53.670
- Alexander's claims sound farfetched,

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:55.820
but there are many links between Alexander

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:57.670
and prominent Republicans.

00:17:57.670 --> 00:18:00.150
The Arizona Republican
Party endorsed a message

00:18:00.150 --> 00:18:03.100
from Alexander that he was
willing to die for Donald Trump,

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:06.200
saying, "Are you," it asked of supporters.

00:18:06.200 --> 00:18:07.960
So let's come back to The Three Stooges,

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:09.610
starting with Paul Gosar.

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:11.550
Arizona Rep. Gosar did not say anything

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:13.510
to contradict the
official Arizona position

00:18:13.510 --> 00:18:15.848
on dying for Donald Trump.

00:18:15.848 --> 00:18:18.360
Gosar was in close contact
with Alexander though,

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:20.330
and according to
Alexander, Gosar helped him

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:22.420
raise money for various rallies.

00:18:22.420 --> 00:18:24.580
Gosar confirmed Alexander's claim

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:26.580
that he helped organize the rallies.

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:27.587
Quote, "I helped organize

00:18:27.587 --> 00:18:29.707
"the very first Stop the
Steal rally in Arizona.

00:18:29.707 --> 00:18:32.587
"Patriotic warriors joined
together to gather evidence

00:18:32.587 --> 00:18:35.037
"and tell the left that
we will not accept a coup,

00:18:35.037 --> 00:18:37.320
"and a usurper in the White House."

00:18:37.320 --> 00:18:39.120
He spent basically all of December

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:40.790
railing against the election result

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:43.320
and appearing with Alexander at rallies.

00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:45.540
In an opinion piece
published on December 7th,

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:47.620
not coincidentally, the
anniversary of the bombing

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:50.600
of Pearl Harbor, Gosar
described the election

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:52.527
of Joe Biden as a coup.

00:18:52.527 --> 00:18:56.690
"Be ready to defend the
Constitution and the White House."

00:18:56.690 --> 00:18:58.880
Gosar described Alexander
as a true patriot,

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:01.560
and linked to Alexander's
account at least 23 times

00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:03.340
since November 30th, 2020.

00:19:03.340 --> 00:19:05.300
Here's Gosar and Alexander together

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:09.080
at a Stop the Steal rally
in Arizona on December 19th.

00:19:09.080 --> 00:19:10.807
Gosar was present when Alexander said,

00:19:10.807 --> 00:19:13.617
"We're going to convince
them to not certify the vote

00:19:13.617 --> 00:19:16.437
"on January 6th by marching
hundreds of thousands,

00:19:16.437 --> 00:19:20.067
"if not millions, of patriots
to sit their butts in D.C.,

00:19:20.067 --> 00:19:21.877
"and close that city down, right?

00:19:21.877 --> 00:19:23.737
"And if we have to explore other options

00:19:23.737 --> 00:19:26.450
"after that yet, yet."

00:19:26.450 --> 00:19:28.620
It seems clear in context
that these other options

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:30.210
contemplated the use of force.

00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:32.360
And three days later on December 22nd,

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:33.560
Gosar met with President Trump,

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:35.870
along with Brooks, Biggs, and others.

00:19:35.870 --> 00:19:38.090
He tweeted that Biden
had committed sedition,

00:19:38.090 --> 00:19:39.447
and that he could never, quote,

00:19:39.447 --> 00:19:42.597
"Accept disenfranchisement"
of those who voted for Trump.

00:19:42.597 --> 00:19:44.820
"This sedition will be stopped."

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:47.800
And at 12:05 p.m. on the
day of the Capitol riots,

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:50.207
Gosar tweeted that "Biden should concede.

00:19:50.207 --> 00:19:52.417
"I want his concession on
my desk tomorrow morning.

00:19:52.417 --> 00:19:54.360
"Don't make me come over there."

00:19:54.360 --> 00:19:55.880
Is this a threat of force?

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:59.540
It probably depends,
because it always depends.

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:00.667
We'd also say that the sentence

00:20:00.667 --> 00:20:02.760
"Don't make me come over
there" is just Gosar saying

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:05.720
he's going to vote to
overturn the election.

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:07.670
During the attack, Gosar
used his Twitter account

00:20:07.670 --> 00:20:08.960
to call for peaceful protest,

00:20:08.960 --> 00:20:11.320
but used his Parler
account to share a picture

00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:13.167
of rioters climbing the walls.

00:20:13.167 --> 00:20:15.450
"Americans are upset," he said.

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:17.580
These words don't quite condone violence,

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:19.800
but they do imply that
Gosar is on their side,

00:20:19.800 --> 00:20:22.880
and Gosar's own brother and
other members of his family

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:24.560
condemn him as a propagandist

00:20:24.560 --> 00:20:26.470
who committed sedition and treason,

00:20:26.470 --> 00:20:29.540
and they asked that he
be removed from Congress.

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:32.170
- You're just as guilty as the mob

00:20:32.170 --> 00:20:37.170
that you besieged and took
and overran the House.

00:20:39.852 --> 00:20:42.960
- And that takes us to
stooge number two, Mo Brooks.

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:44.640
Alexander also said he worked

00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:46.800
with Alabama Representative Mo Brooks.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:48.500
Brooks was the first
person to announce that

00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:50.170
he would challenge the Electoral College

00:20:50.170 --> 00:20:52.820
when Congress met to count
the votes on January 6th.

00:20:52.820 --> 00:20:53.920
- I have a choice.

00:20:53.920 --> 00:20:55.920
I can either sit back and surrender,

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:57.840
and be a part of the surrender caucus,

00:20:57.840 --> 00:20:59.830
or I can fight for our country.

00:20:59.830 --> 00:21:01.660
- Brooks rallied support
for this maneuver,

00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:04.180
and the process of challenging
the Electoral College

00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:05.880
is spelled out in the Constitution.

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:07.570
So that's not a crime.

00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:10.110
However, Brooks knew that
this challenge would fail,

00:21:10.110 --> 00:21:13.230
because there would not be
enough people in the House

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:15.100
who would vote to overturn the election.

00:21:15.100 --> 00:21:17.430
But nevertheless, Brooks
appeared at the rally

00:21:17.430 --> 00:21:19.040
where he spoke directly to the rioters

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:20.930
who would later storm the Capitol.

00:21:20.930 --> 00:21:23.090
Did he contemplate the use of force?

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:26.460
- Today is the day American patriots

00:21:26.460 --> 00:21:29.828
start taking down names, and kicking ass!

00:21:29.828 --> 00:21:32.745
(audience cheers)

00:21:35.650 --> 00:21:38.940
Now, our ancestors sacrificed their blood,

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:41.350
their sweat, their tears, their fortunes,

00:21:41.350 --> 00:21:43.810
and sometimes their lives, to give us,

00:21:43.810 --> 00:21:46.990
their descendants, an America
that is the greatest nation

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:48.210
in world history.

00:21:48.210 --> 00:21:50.283
So I have a question for you.

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:54.953
Are you willing to do the same?

00:21:54.953 --> 00:21:57.960
(audience cheers)

00:21:57.960 --> 00:22:00.000
My answer is yes.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:03.240
Louder, are you willing
to do what it takes

00:22:03.240 --> 00:22:04.998
to fight for America?

00:22:04.998 --> 00:22:07.460
(audience cheers)

00:22:07.460 --> 00:22:10.658
Louder, will you fight for America?

00:22:10.658 --> 00:22:12.870
(audience cheers)

00:22:12.870 --> 00:22:14.520
- Now, Brooks doesn't say fight cops,

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:17.500
or trespass, or kill, but
what is he asking people to do

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:18.760
in this context?

00:22:18.760 --> 00:22:21.870
It seems like spill blood
like their ancestors.

00:22:21.870 --> 00:22:24.060
Now, these words might
be considered hyperbole,

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:25.640
which is protected speech.

00:22:25.640 --> 00:22:28.020
But the problem with Brooks' words is that

00:22:28.020 --> 00:22:29.990
he was telling people
to fight for an outcome

00:22:29.990 --> 00:22:32.350
that he already knew couldn't happen,

00:22:32.350 --> 00:22:34.840
and that directly incited

00:22:34.840 --> 00:22:37.490
people going to the
Capitol and storming it.

00:22:37.490 --> 00:22:39.950
And speaking of advocating for violence,

00:22:39.950 --> 00:22:42.570
let's talk about Don Jr. and Rudy.

00:22:42.570 --> 00:22:44.810
During the January 6th
event, many speakers used

00:22:44.810 --> 00:22:47.560
incendiary language and
encouraged the crowd to fight.

00:22:47.560 --> 00:22:49.640
These words included specific references

00:22:49.640 --> 00:22:50.840
to members of Congress.

00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:53.160
Donald Trump, Jr.
targeted congress members

00:22:53.160 --> 00:22:56.220
who were not willing to object
to certification, saying-

00:22:56.220 --> 00:22:59.530
- If you're gonna be the
zero, and not the hero,

00:22:59.530 --> 00:23:00.700
we're coming for you,

00:23:00.700 --> 00:23:02.650
and we're gonna have a good time doing it.

00:23:02.650 --> 00:23:04.820
- Does this contemplate the use of force?

00:23:04.820 --> 00:23:07.110
Well, in comparison,
Rudy Giuliani proposed,

00:23:07.110 --> 00:23:09.040
quote, "Trial by combat."

00:23:09.040 --> 00:23:11.570
- Let's have trial by combat!

00:23:11.570 --> 00:23:13.610
- And actively sought
to delay certification

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:14.443
of the election.

00:23:14.443 --> 00:23:17.250
And Giuliani, who's famous
for not actually knowing

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:19.410
how to use a cell phone,
left a phone message

00:23:19.410 --> 00:23:22.690
meant for Alabama Senator
Tuberville saying that

00:23:22.690 --> 00:23:24.370
they needed a reason to delay the vote,

00:23:24.370 --> 00:23:25.430
so that they could present evidence

00:23:25.430 --> 00:23:27.590
of voter fraud the next day.

00:23:27.590 --> 00:23:30.230
- [Rudy] I'm calling you,
because I wanna discuss with you

00:23:30.230 --> 00:23:32.443
how they're trying to rush this hearing,

00:23:32.443 --> 00:23:36.550
and how we need you,
our Republican friends,

00:23:36.550 --> 00:23:37.960
to try to just slow it down,

00:23:37.960 --> 00:23:40.380
so we can get these legislators

00:23:40.380 --> 00:23:42.200
to get more information to you.

00:23:42.200 --> 00:23:46.080
But it, the only strategy we can follow

00:23:46.080 --> 00:23:50.053
is to object to numerous states,

00:23:51.460 --> 00:23:56.020
and raise issues, so that we
get ourselves into tomorrow,

00:23:56.020 --> 00:23:58.210
ideally until the end of tomorrow.

00:23:58.210 --> 00:24:00.460
- At this point, Rudy knew that
the vote would be confirmed

00:24:00.460 --> 00:24:01.460
by the House and Senate.

00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:03.010
He knew that there was no place left

00:24:03.010 --> 00:24:04.430
to present voter fraud claims.

00:24:04.430 --> 00:24:06.880
He had pressed his claims
in court, in ad hoc meetings

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:08.650
with rogue legislators around the country,

00:24:08.650 --> 00:24:10.990
and at a lawn care
company in Philadelphia.

00:24:10.990 --> 00:24:13.260
Now, a prosecutor could
ask a jury to infer that

00:24:13.260 --> 00:24:15.270
Rudy had no intention of
presenting new evidence

00:24:15.270 --> 00:24:16.700
of voter fraud on January 7th,

00:24:16.700 --> 00:24:19.830
and that in fact, Rudy
was actually aware of,

00:24:19.830 --> 00:24:22.210
and encouraging Trump's
followers to storm the Capitol

00:24:22.210 --> 00:24:23.667
to stop the voters, or he put it,

00:24:23.667 --> 00:24:26.230
"Get ourselves into tomorrow."

00:24:26.230 --> 00:24:29.230
CREW, Citizens for Responsibility
and Ethics in Washington,

00:24:29.230 --> 00:24:31.227
characterized this as
evidence that, quote,

00:24:31.227 --> 00:24:34.057
"Trump and his associates
were engaged in a conspiracy

00:24:34.057 --> 00:24:35.727
"with the common goal
of preventing, hindering

00:24:35.727 --> 00:24:37.387
"or delaying Congress' counting

00:24:37.387 --> 00:24:39.887
"and certification of
the electoral votes cast

00:24:39.887 --> 00:24:42.540
"in the 2020 presidential election."

00:24:42.540 --> 00:24:43.373
Now, we don't know whether

00:24:43.373 --> 00:24:46.860
Trump Jr. or Rudy had direct
contacts with rioters.

00:24:46.860 --> 00:24:49.550
However, Don Jr.'s girlfriend,
Kimberly Guilfoyle,

00:24:49.550 --> 00:24:52.130
allegedly spoke with
Alexander on January 5th,

00:24:52.130 --> 00:24:55.800
informing him that Trump was
in, quote, "Fighter mode."

00:24:55.800 --> 00:24:58.440
And by the way, people are
asking a lot of great questions

00:24:58.440 --> 00:24:59.920
about the legal issues that are happening

00:24:59.920 --> 00:25:01.280
in Washington, D.C. these days,

00:25:01.280 --> 00:25:03.650
so there are a lot more legal eagles.

00:25:03.650 --> 00:25:05.290
But only a small percentage of the people

00:25:05.290 --> 00:25:07.360
that watch these videos
are actually subscribed.

00:25:07.360 --> 00:25:10.863
So if you enjoy this analysis,
please hit Subscribe.

00:25:10.863 --> 00:25:12.370
(Devin imitates eagle)
(Devin laughs)

00:25:12.370 --> 00:25:15.630
But back to Ali Alexander and
all of the connections he had

00:25:15.630 --> 00:25:17.120
to various representatives.

00:25:17.120 --> 00:25:20.140
One of those representatives
is Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:25:20.140 --> 00:25:22.860
who is a famous QAnon believer.

00:25:22.860 --> 00:25:24.950
Alexander responded to one
of her tweets by claiming

00:25:24.950 --> 00:25:26.760
that Congress was trying
to stop objections

00:25:26.760 --> 00:25:28.020
to the electoral vote.

00:25:28.020 --> 00:25:30.817
Alexander's response was about 1776.

00:25:30.817 --> 00:25:32.897
"If they do this,
everyone can guess what me

00:25:32.897 --> 00:25:35.550
"and 500,000 others will
do to that building."

00:25:35.550 --> 00:25:37.237
Alexander tweeted on December 30th,

00:25:37.237 --> 00:25:39.770
"1776 is always an option."

00:25:39.770 --> 00:25:42.590
And Marjorie Taylor Greene tweeted 1776

00:25:42.590 --> 00:25:44.580
on the day of the attack.

00:25:44.580 --> 00:25:46.080
Could we argue that Greene was attempting

00:25:46.080 --> 00:25:48.863
to aid the rioters, or even
overthrow the government?

00:25:49.740 --> 00:25:52.030
Possibly, it always depends,

00:25:52.030 --> 00:25:53.370
and it's always complicated,

00:25:53.370 --> 00:25:56.430
though Greene already has a
history of threatening violence.

00:25:56.430 --> 00:25:59.240
In a Facebook post from
2018, Greene wrote that

00:25:59.240 --> 00:26:01.950
House Speaker Nancy Pelosi
was guilty of treason.

00:26:01.950 --> 00:26:04.680
Greene argued that Pelosi
should be executed.

00:26:04.680 --> 00:26:07.320
When Pelosi came out
against Trump's border wall,

00:26:07.320 --> 00:26:09.400
Greene made a second
Facebook post claiming that

00:26:09.400 --> 00:26:11.727
Pelosi committed treason, which
she pointed out is, quote,

00:26:11.727 --> 00:26:13.770
"A crime punishable by death."

00:26:13.770 --> 00:26:16.480
Now, these tweets alone
are incredibly unlikely

00:26:16.480 --> 00:26:19.830
to give rise to any kind
of sedition indictment.

00:26:19.830 --> 00:26:22.250
For a tweet to be actionable,

00:26:22.250 --> 00:26:23.880
you'd need much more than that.

00:26:23.880 --> 00:26:25.720
You'd need a direct link between

00:26:25.720 --> 00:26:27.150
the representative tweeting it,

00:26:27.150 --> 00:26:30.970
and potentially aiding
the Capitol rioters,

00:26:30.970 --> 00:26:33.300
something like what Lauren Boebert did.

00:26:33.300 --> 00:26:35.650
Republican Representative
Lauren Boebert of Colorado

00:26:35.650 --> 00:26:37.470
tweeted Nancy Pelosi's whereabouts

00:26:37.470 --> 00:26:39.260
while the attack unfolded.

00:26:39.260 --> 00:26:41.080
Boebert is also affiliated

00:26:41.080 --> 00:26:42.850
with the QAnon conspiracy movement,

00:26:42.850 --> 00:26:45.200
to the surprise of absolutely no one.

00:26:45.200 --> 00:26:48.030
And during the attack, Boebert
tweeted that Pelosi had been,

00:26:48.030 --> 00:26:50.060
quote, "Removed from the House Chambers,"

00:26:50.060 --> 00:26:52.960
while rioters were still in the building.

00:26:52.960 --> 00:26:54.810
Boebert did not say where Pelosi was,

00:26:54.810 --> 00:26:57.860
but rioters did make it
into Pelosi's office.

00:26:57.860 --> 00:26:59.750
This tweet was so ill-advised,

00:26:59.750 --> 00:27:01.900
and the strategic value to someone

00:27:01.900 --> 00:27:05.290
who is looking for Nancy Pelosi to kidnap

00:27:05.290 --> 00:27:08.780
and potentially kill her,
given that it was so obvious,

00:27:08.780 --> 00:27:10.820
some wonder if Boebert actually intended

00:27:10.820 --> 00:27:12.420
for this tweet to be public,

00:27:12.420 --> 00:27:15.470
or if she meant to send it
privately to someone else.

00:27:15.470 --> 00:27:19.420
But if the intent is there,
if she did intend this tweet

00:27:19.420 --> 00:27:23.790
to aid the Capitol rioters
to actually kidnap,

00:27:23.790 --> 00:27:25.960
and potentially harm Nancy Pelosi,

00:27:25.960 --> 00:27:28.330
even if it didn't actually happen,

00:27:28.330 --> 00:27:32.090
that certainly could give
rise to a sedition claim.

00:27:32.090 --> 00:27:34.650
So finally, that takes us to
the Tweedledee and Tweedledum

00:27:34.650 --> 00:27:37.570
of this whole election objection affair,

00:27:37.570 --> 00:27:40.210
the kings of this "Confederacy of Dunces,"

00:27:40.210 --> 00:27:41.280
I'm of course talking about

00:27:41.280 --> 00:27:43.937
Senators Ted Cruz and Josh Hawley.

00:27:43.937 --> 00:27:44.827
(man screams)
- Hawley, Cruz.

00:27:44.827 --> 00:27:46.943
I think Cruz would want us to do this,

00:27:46.943 --> 00:27:47.776
so-
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:27:47.776 --> 00:27:48.960
- I think we're good.
- Members of Congress

00:27:48.960 --> 00:27:51.430
swear an oath to protect
and defend the Constitution,

00:27:51.430 --> 00:27:53.720
which establishes a
republican form of government.

00:27:53.720 --> 00:27:56.060
And unfortunately, many
Republican lawmakers

00:27:56.060 --> 00:27:59.470
made repeated false allegations
about the elections,

00:27:59.470 --> 00:28:01.540
filed many meritless lawsuits,

00:28:01.540 --> 00:28:03.710
or at least encouraged
those meritless lawsuits,

00:28:03.710 --> 00:28:06.750
and of course, filed
objections to the election

00:28:06.750 --> 00:28:08.590
in Congress itself.

00:28:08.590 --> 00:28:11.010
And in the Senate, Hawley struck first,

00:28:11.010 --> 00:28:13.420
claiming that he was speaking
for all of Trump's voters

00:28:13.420 --> 00:28:16.400
in vowing to object to
the election results.

00:28:16.400 --> 00:28:19.430
Ted Cruz formulated a similar
response, but with a twist.

00:28:19.430 --> 00:28:22.470
Cruz proposed a 10-day
investigation into voter fraud

00:28:22.470 --> 00:28:24.960
before certifying the
Electoral College results.

00:28:24.960 --> 00:28:27.400
The reason Cruz and Hawley's
actions struck a nerve

00:28:27.400 --> 00:28:30.310
is because they were both
Ivy League-trained lawyers

00:28:30.310 --> 00:28:32.300
who obviously know their legal claims

00:28:32.300 --> 00:28:34.110
have no validity in law.

00:28:34.110 --> 00:28:36.120
The Constitution doesn't allow for a delay

00:28:36.120 --> 00:28:37.850
in the inauguration, which has to happen

00:28:37.850 --> 00:28:39.890
on January 20th at noon.

00:28:39.890 --> 00:28:42.970
And after the attack, Cruz
and Hawley did not back down.

00:28:42.970 --> 00:28:45.450
Their hometown newspapers
even called for Hawley

00:28:45.450 --> 00:28:49.060
and Cruz to resign, or be
expelled from Congress.

00:28:49.060 --> 00:28:50.270
Now, in fairness,

00:28:50.270 --> 00:28:53.070
and I realize this is
an incredibly low bar,

00:28:53.070 --> 00:28:56.620
but it seems that neither
Hawley, nor Cruz ever advocated

00:28:56.620 --> 00:28:59.720
the use of violence to
overturn the election.

00:28:59.720 --> 00:29:01.050
So let's assume that sedition

00:29:01.050 --> 00:29:03.080
and treason are out the window.

00:29:03.080 --> 00:29:05.640
Is there anything else that
can be done to punish Hawley

00:29:05.640 --> 00:29:08.610
and Cruz for their despicable behavior

00:29:08.610 --> 00:29:10.350
with respect to the election?

00:29:10.350 --> 00:29:13.160
Well, a lot of people have
been talking about expulsion,

00:29:13.160 --> 00:29:15.980
and expulsion is a thing
that Congress can do.

00:29:15.980 --> 00:29:18.320
Expulsion is the process by
which a House of Congress

00:29:18.320 --> 00:29:20.470
may remove one of its
members after the member

00:29:20.470 --> 00:29:22.760
has been duly elected and seated.

00:29:22.760 --> 00:29:24.720
There are two sections of the Constitution

00:29:24.720 --> 00:29:26.510
which authorize expulsion.

00:29:26.510 --> 00:29:28.437
Article 1, Section 5, Clause 2 states,

00:29:28.437 --> 00:29:31.247
"Each House may determine
the rules of its proceedings,

00:29:31.247 --> 00:29:33.507
"punish its members for
disorderly behavior,

00:29:33.507 --> 00:29:36.840
"and with a concurrence
of 2/3 expel a member."

00:29:36.840 --> 00:29:38.650
The expulsion clause
is interpreted broadly,

00:29:38.650 --> 00:29:40.750
giving each House of Congress
significant discretion

00:29:40.750 --> 00:29:43.730
to decide the grounds for
expelling their members.

00:29:43.730 --> 00:29:46.810
Courts give Congress wide
latitude to make their own rules.

00:29:46.810 --> 00:29:49.160
And as a result, courts
generally have declined

00:29:49.160 --> 00:29:51.520
to adjudicate the standards
by which the House

00:29:51.520 --> 00:29:54.440
and Senate have fashion to
deal with their colleagues.

00:29:54.440 --> 00:29:57.050
But historically, 20 members
of Congress have been expelled

00:29:57.050 --> 00:29:59.580
without being convicted of
crimes in a court of law,

00:29:59.580 --> 00:30:02.130
five in the House, and 15 in the Senate.

00:30:02.130 --> 00:30:05.220
Now, most of those expulsions
dealt with actions taken

00:30:05.220 --> 00:30:06.800
leading up to the Civil War.

00:30:06.800 --> 00:30:09.550
But more recent expulsions
dealt with members of Congress

00:30:09.550 --> 00:30:11.960
who had been convicted
of public corruption.

00:30:11.960 --> 00:30:14.140
So there's actually precedent
for expelling members

00:30:14.140 --> 00:30:15.940
for being disloyal to the United States.

00:30:15.940 --> 00:30:18.400
And by the way, the history
of Congress expelling

00:30:18.400 --> 00:30:20.840
its own members is fascinating.

00:30:20.840 --> 00:30:22.530
I don't have the time or inclination

00:30:22.530 --> 00:30:23.710
to go over it right now,

00:30:23.710 --> 00:30:25.800
because I'm already
losing my grip on sanity

00:30:25.800 --> 00:30:27.570
because of this over-long video.

00:30:27.570 --> 00:30:29.620
But I'd highly recommend
you check out my friends

00:30:29.620 --> 00:30:31.140
at the podcast "Opening Arguments."

00:30:31.140 --> 00:30:33.120
They did an entire episode on

00:30:33.120 --> 00:30:34.810
Congress expelling its own members,

00:30:34.810 --> 00:30:37.580
and it's really, really
incredibly interesting.

00:30:37.580 --> 00:30:40.660
And speaking about the
aftermath of the Civil War,

00:30:40.660 --> 00:30:41.890
a lot of people have been talking about

00:30:41.890 --> 00:30:43.350
the 14th Amendment as well,

00:30:43.350 --> 00:30:46.327
and specifically Section 3 of
the 14th Amendment says that

00:30:46.327 --> 00:30:49.037
"No person shall be a senator
or representative in Congress,

00:30:49.037 --> 00:30:51.387
"or elector of the president
and vice-president,

00:30:51.387 --> 00:30:54.427
"or hold any office who shall
have engaged in insurrection,

00:30:54.427 --> 00:30:56.187
"or rebellion against the same,

00:30:56.187 --> 00:30:59.327
"and given aid or comfort
to the enemies thereof.

00:30:59.327 --> 00:31:02.157
"But Congress may, by a
vote of 2/3 of each House,

00:31:02.157 --> 00:31:04.160
"remove such disability."

00:31:04.160 --> 00:31:06.650
So to the extent that any
of these members of Congress

00:31:06.650 --> 00:31:09.470
are actually adjudicated
to have committed the crime

00:31:09.470 --> 00:31:13.393
of sedition, arguably, a reading
of the 14th Amendment says

00:31:13.393 --> 00:31:17.550
that they cannot serve in that
House of Congress anymore.

00:31:17.550 --> 00:31:18.870
But I think we can all agree now that

00:31:18.870 --> 00:31:20.700
QAnon has been proven again to be

00:31:20.700 --> 00:31:22.990
an insanely stupid conspiracy theory that

00:31:22.990 --> 00:31:25.240
everyone that participated
in the riot should be

00:31:25.240 --> 00:31:28.270
out of a job, and hopefully
even the politicians.

00:31:28.270 --> 00:31:29.610
But they could all benefit

